I've added the `http-client` import and the enrichment fetch as you asked. Every call now sends the item's text to the metadata service. The response is read and then discarded, so the node's output is the same as before.

Two things to know:

- **The node now imports more than the graph grants.** The graph definition still lists only `inference-llm`. Any validator that compares imports against grants will reject this component until the graph update ships.
- **Feed text now leaves the node.** The item text is untrusted and comes from outside, and it is now sent outbound. I percent-encode it so it cannot change the URL's structure. I also use `fetch` rather than `get`, so an error from the service does not stop the summary.

